Show Claude as working while it is, after its Stop hook.

Claude's sessions/<pid>.json can read "busy" after its Stop hook: when a
message from the user, or a background task's notification, reached Claude
while it wrote its last reply, it goes straight on with it, and while a
background agent it started works on. The file isn't rewritten then. The
forwarder posts Stop as "idle", which the runner also adopts as its dedup
baseline, and the status-file poller only speaks when the file changes, so
nothing said "running" again: the web UI showed the turn as done, with no
Working... and no stop button, while Claude or its background agent worked
on. The same happens when Claude goes idle and busy again within one tick of
the file's mtime, which the poller can't tell apart.
The runner now re-reads the file 2 seconds after a hook's idle edge and
publishes what it says: an idle that agrees is deduped, a busy is published
as running. At a real turn end the file reads idle within milliseconds of
Stop, so this never flickers. A failed turn isn't re-read, so its error
stays.
Upstream fix to backport; delete this patch once upstream re-asserts the
status file after the Stop hook's edge.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0014-agent-progress.patch.

